WEBVTT

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:27.750
<b>LEGEND</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:27.750
<b>OF THE</b>

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:27.750
<b>  GALACTIC HEROES</b>

00:01:53.330 --> 00:02:01.750
The Mutineer
Chapter III

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:07.700
On September 2nd
of Imperial Year 482...

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:12.000
...the destroyer, Hameln II,
was facing a grave crisis.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:17.020
Well, I summoned you here for a reason.

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:19.450
We're having trouble repairing
the engine, and even if we fix it...

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:22.720
...it seems we'll have
problems with acceleration.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:24.900
On top of that, we've
confirmed that the enemy fleet...

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:29.300
...consists not only of slow battleships and cruisers, but also fighter craft.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:36.080
I'll tell you my decision first: as
things stand now, we can't escape.

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:39.530
At this point, we must take action in
accordance with military regulations.

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:41.540
That's my decision.

00:02:42.060 --> 00:02:44.000
Action in accordance
with military regulations ?

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.150
You don't mean...?

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.950
To prevent the leakage
of military secrets...

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:52.090
...we will self-destruct.

00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:58.100
The self-destruct procedure usually requires the agreement of the top three officers.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:01.760
Normally, those are the captain,
first officer, and chief navigator.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.700
But since we're
lacking two of them...

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:07.900
...the three of us, the chief gunner,
the chief missileer, and I, should...

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.300
Please wait...

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:13.150
Um, I'm reluctant to say this,
but how about surrendering...

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:16.230
Imperial military regulations
do not allow for surrender !

00:03:16.570 --> 00:03:19.350
But in reality, that regulation
is no longer observed...

00:03:19.350 --> 00:03:22.060
...and there have been
many cases of surrender...

00:03:22.060 --> 00:03:25.900
I choose dignified death rather than disgraceful surrender.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:29.930
That is to uphold my pride as an
honorable Imperial military officer.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:31.100
B...but...

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:32.810
Think about it.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:35.850
In the absence of the aristocrat captain and chief navigator...

00:03:35.850 --> 00:03:39.800
...if we, the commoners,
decide to surrender our ship...

00:03:39.800 --> 00:03:45.490
...we'll definitely be ridiculed as commoners who have no pride, no self-respect.

00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:49.470
I have always behaved as a
paragon of the Imperial Fleet.

00:03:49.470 --> 00:03:51.900
It is my duty to fulfill that role.

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:55.900
It's a serious decision,
so I won't rush you.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:59.350
But if we're discovered by the enemy we'll have to make a choice whether we like it or not.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:02.400
I want you to make up
your mind before that happens.

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:12.210
The First Officer is planning to self-destruct
if we're found by the enemy and can't escape.

00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.900
What ?

00:04:13.900 --> 00:04:15.210
I recommended surrender.

00:04:16.610 --> 00:04:17.850
Even if we're captured...

00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:23.190
...the brass would give LTJG Musel priority in a prisoner exchange to arrange for his return.

00:04:23.190 --> 00:04:25.660
And we might benefit
from that as well.

00:04:25.660 --> 00:04:32.140
But the First Officer is extremely hung up on
being blamed for his class{i.e. commoner} if things go wrong.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:35.090
He thinks he'd rather die
than be blamed for his class.

00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:36.770
That's sick.

00:04:36.770 --> 00:04:39.170
Then what do you plan to do ?

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:40.600
It's up to LTJG Musel.

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:46.410
If I were held accountable for mutiny, I have no connections that could give me support.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:49.020
But if it's LTJG Musel...

00:04:49.020 --> 00:04:52.040
So you'd rather have someone
else pick up the chestnut in fire ?

00:04:52.040 --> 00:04:53.660
Don't say that.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:57.750
If LTJG Musel stands up against
the First Officer, I will cooperate.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:00.500
I'm sure Shamissoe is
against self-destruction, too.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:05.080
If three chiefs cooperate, we might be able to overturn the First Officer's authority.

00:05:05.080 --> 00:05:08.290
But that requires
some forceful action first.

00:05:08.290 --> 00:05:10.650
That's why I'm talking
to the Security Chief{i.e. Kircheis}.

00:05:14.530 --> 00:05:16.400
The security officers
are my subordinates...

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.730
...but most of them are closely
associated with the First Officer.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:19.710
I wonder what I should do.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.060
Watch Ensign Kircheis.

00:05:32.060 --> 00:05:34.370
If you see any suspicious activities, report them to me right away.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:35.060
Yes, sir.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.340
Well, we took a shot in a nasty spot...

00:05:58.340 --> 00:05:59.240
Petty Officer Zaidel.

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:02.040
Petty Officer Zaidel, I'm up here.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:07.440
Oh, it's the Ensign.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.760
What are you doing up there ?

00:06:09.450 --> 00:06:11.550
Don't move, just listen to me.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:16.940
I understand the situation.

00:06:16.940 --> 00:06:18.000
But what are you going to do ?

00:06:19.740 --> 00:06:21.960
I will rescue LTJG Musel.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:25.490
Then I will follow
LTJG Musel's orders.

00:06:25.490 --> 00:06:28.550
What do you mean, "then" ?
That's already an act of mutiny.

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:30.450
There's no going back.

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:33.610
Don't get me wrong.

00:06:33.610 --> 00:06:36.330
I really like you guys.

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:39.820
But I've been with
the First Officer longer.

00:06:39.820 --> 00:06:42.170
He's taken care of us many times.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:44.680
I just can't betray him that easily.

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:47.170
I'm not telling you to
betray the First Officer.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:50.510
I just want you to make a choice that allows us to return alive.

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.570
But the First Officer has
been in space for five years.

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:55.600
No matter how
brilliant LTJG Musel is...

00:06:55.600 --> 00:06:58.250
...there's a difference in the
amount of experience they have.

00:06:58.250 --> 00:07:00.990
The First Officer has
already made a mistake.

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:06.150
If he had taken command, this ship
would already be space debris.

00:07:07.190 --> 00:07:09.050
Not only that...

00:07:09.050 --> 00:07:11.700
...he seems to be planning to self-destruct, in accordance with military regulations.

00:07:13.170 --> 00:07:15.370
But that's as a last resort, right ?

00:07:15.370 --> 00:07:18.010
But the First Officer
has no escape plan.

00:07:18.010 --> 00:07:21.200
As it is, self-destruction
is our predetermined path.

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:26.360
I ask for your cooperation.

00:07:26.360 --> 00:07:28.400
The fate of everyone on
this ship depends on it.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:35.380
I understand.

00:07:35.380 --> 00:07:36.650
But I'll at least ask
you not to interfere.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:39.890
Damn it all.

00:07:40.750 --> 00:07:41.940
Hey, Rolf !

00:07:48.460 --> 00:07:49.140
Open the door.

00:07:49.140 --> 00:07:50.370
We can't.

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:52.630
We were ordered
not to let anyone in.

00:07:52.630 --> 00:07:55.820
I believe I was the one who
ordered the surveillance here.

00:07:55.820 --> 00:07:57.620
The First Officer's order has priority.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:02.930
The First Officer ordered us that if Ensign Kircheis attempted to contact LTJG Musel...

00:08:02.930 --> 00:08:06.900
...we should consider the act as tantamount to mutiny and should arrest you.

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:12.880
If you fire in a narrow hallway like this,
you'll end up shooting your own people.

00:08:36.750 --> 00:08:37.100
Give me that...

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:41.910
Sorry.

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:48.550
Petty Officer...

00:08:49.030 --> 00:08:51.270
Having too many members wouldn't do us much good.

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:53.250
A trustworthy group of
four or five should do.

00:08:54.440 --> 00:08:57.610
But in any case, Ensign,
you're pretty strong.

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:01.260
LTJG Musel is even
stronger than I am.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:04.500
All right then, shall we
ask for his appearance ?

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:21.050
Let us go.

00:09:21.050 --> 00:09:22.600
We'll take over the bridge.

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:41.860
What do you think you're doing ?

00:09:41.860 --> 00:09:43.180
Just as you see.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:47.000
In order for us to escape the
present situation, I will take command.

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:48.350
That's absurd.

00:09:48.350 --> 00:09:49.980
And you, too.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:51.680
I'm sorry, Sir.

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:53.900
But we want to survive, too.

00:09:53.900 --> 00:09:57.620
And for that, it seems better if LTJG Musel takes command.

00:09:58.300 --> 00:09:59.740
Everyone thinks so, right ?

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:08.480
I agree.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:10.700
I support LTJG Musel.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:14.070
Hey, Dewling, are you planning to participate in a mutiny ?

00:10:14.070 --> 00:10:15.900
I don't think this is a mutiny.

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:17.470
This is for our own survival.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:21.600
But even if we return home alive, you'll be court-martialed.

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:23.180
Think about it.

00:10:23.180 --> 00:10:26.850
LTJG Musel is the brother
of Countess Grünewald.

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:31.230
Even if we are court-martialed,
it'll all be taken care of.

00:10:32.050 --> 00:10:34.980
It's for our own good
to support LTJG Musel.

00:10:36.380 --> 00:10:41.500
In any case, even though the First Officer
doesn't appear inclined to surrender command...

00:10:41.500 --> 00:10:45.210
...I will take control of the
bridge with this blaster{i.e. his gun}.

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:49.800
If you side with the First Officer we will detain you, along with him, but we do not plan to harm you.

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:54.400
If you remain neutral, I ask you only to focus on your own job.

00:10:54.400 --> 00:10:56.610
I can't agree with an act like this.

00:10:56.610 --> 00:10:58.910
I will definitely side
with the First Officer.

00:10:58.910 --> 00:11:00.450
I have to fix the engine.

00:11:00.450 --> 00:11:01.960
I won't side with either of you.

00:11:01.960 --> 00:11:03.230
That's fine.

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:05.190
Then I'll remain neutral, too.

00:11:05.190 --> 00:11:07.300
I support LTJG Musel.

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:10.280
I will concentrate on my own tasks.

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:11.910
All right.

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:14.660
We will detain the First Officer
and Ensign Emerich.

00:11:14.660 --> 00:11:16.760
I will assume command
from this point on.

00:11:16.760 --> 00:11:17.650
Take them away.

00:11:18.970 --> 00:11:21.010
LTJG Musel, you'll regret this.

00:11:22.370 --> 00:11:24.950
If we die, there's no
chance to regret anything.

00:11:29.450 --> 00:11:31.770
Ensign Kircheis, remain here.

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:33.650
Petty Officer, I leave you in charge.

00:11:38.910 --> 00:11:41.820
Kircheis, watch my back.

00:11:41.820 --> 00:11:44.150
Not everyone here is my ally yet.

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.600
Yes, Lord Reinhard.

00:11:46.910 --> 00:11:50.650
Reinhard became interested in Schmitt's
plan upon hearing about it from Kircheis...

00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:53.280
...and started to iron out
the details of the plan.

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:58.550
Even if I were to adopt this plan, the
engine repairs still need to be completed.

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:01.630
What's the expected time
of the next surface explosion ?

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.210
It's 17 hours from now.

00:12:03.210 --> 00:12:06.300
If we miss it, we'll have 
to wait another 62 hours.

00:12:07.260 --> 00:12:09.110
That'll be too late.

00:12:09.110 --> 00:12:12.160
The possibility of being discovered by the enemy will be too high.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:15.250
Assuming we will use the
explosion 17 hours from now...

00:12:15.250 --> 00:12:18.270
...reverse-calculate the
starting time of free fall.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:21.680
If we don't start the operation three hours from now, we won't make it.

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:23.800
We can't fix the
engine in three hours.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:27.790
As long as the engine is fixed within 17 hours, it'll be fine.

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:31.550
But once we start the
operation, we can't abort.

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:35.660
Once it's started, we can't go back even if we find out the engine can't be fixed...

00:12:35.660 --> 00:12:38.970
No, if we have 17 hours,
we'll be all right.

00:12:38.970 --> 00:12:41.520
With maximum effort from
the engineering crew, that is.

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:48.250
Either way, I'll ask you to concentrate
your best efforts on repairing the engine.

00:12:48.250 --> 00:12:50.530
I will return your subordinates
I had borrowed, also.

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.270
That's what I'd ask.

00:12:52.270 --> 00:12:54.790
Though I don't remember lending them to you to begin with.

00:12:54.790 --> 00:12:57.050
Hey, Schmitt, let's go.

00:12:57.050 --> 00:12:57.700
Y...yes.

00:13:04.200 --> 00:13:07.600
Do you think it'll be all right,
with that lazy engineering crew ?

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:10.560
Watch your words !

00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.100
What do you plan to do ?

00:13:14.100 --> 00:13:17.750
Will we adopt
Seaman Schmitt's plan ?

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:19.450
That's what I intend to do.

00:13:19.450 --> 00:13:21.700
But it's too risky.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.440
I know the risk.

00:13:23.440 --> 00:13:24.740
And there are no other plans.

00:13:24.740 --> 00:13:27.630
But to depend on just one soldier ?

00:13:27.630 --> 00:13:31.520
He may be "just one soldier" in the military, but astrophysics is his expertise.

00:13:31.520 --> 00:13:34.700
His observation data
is detailed and reliable.

00:13:34.700 --> 00:13:37.510
But there's no guarantee that
the engine will be fixed in time...

00:13:37.510 --> 00:13:39.860
I trust them.

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:41.550
If you can't trust your subordinates, you can't fight a war.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:50.210
The door is locked, but
it seems there's no guard.

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:54.000
I don't suppose they can afford to spare the manpower for an extraneous task.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:13:59.800
Sir.

00:13:59.800 --> 00:14:00.710
Where{are you communicating} from ?

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:02.540
From my room.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:05.640
I created a bypass on my computer
system and made a forceful connection.

00:14:05.640 --> 00:14:06.380
All right.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:07.100
What's happening ?

00:14:10.550 --> 00:14:12.310
I understand the situation.

00:14:12.310 --> 00:14:14.360
Just as I thought,
Musel is an amateur.

00:14:14.360 --> 00:14:18.010
He can't even distinguish between
reality and airy armchair theories.

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:20.450
I have to take command of the ship back.

00:14:20.870 --> 00:14:21.910
What do we do ?

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:23.130
Get some allies.

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:24.210
We won't need much.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:25.710
And weapons.

00:14:25.710 --> 00:14:29.140
Ensign Kircheis has taken control of the weaponry, so it may be difficult to obtain them.

00:14:30.080 --> 00:14:33.960
We can get laser torches for outboard work and liquid oxygen cylinders.

00:14:33.960 --> 00:14:36.790
We can use them for close combat.

00:14:36.790 --> 00:14:38.680
And we can burn the lock, too.

00:14:38.680 --> 00:14:39.990
Order acknowledged.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:52.030
Hey, don't shoot.

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:56.850
What do you plan to do ?

00:14:56.850 --> 00:14:59.810
As you can see,
I'm taking him hostage.

00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:04.600
You intend to take advantage of the life of your subordinate as a pawn ?

00:15:06.700 --> 00:15:09.480
He's not a subordinate
anymore, he's a mutineer !

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:11.190
Musel, that goes for you, too.

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:14.270
So disarm now and
return command of the ship.

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:15.760
Hey...

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:20.190
If I return command, 
what do you intend to do ?

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:23.400
I will take an action that I can feel proud of as an Imperial military serviceman.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:26.730
Does that mean you
will scuttle this ship ?

00:15:26.730 --> 00:15:30.900
And you're planning to have
this ship dive into this system's star.

00:15:30.900 --> 00:15:33.940
Rather than putting up such useless struggles and disgracefully incinerating ourselves...

00:15:33.940 --> 00:15:39.060
...we can preserve our honor by courageously embracing our self-determined "end."

00:15:39.060 --> 00:15:42.250
So you plan to take the lives of many
soldiers just for your own self-satisfaction...

00:15:42.250 --> 00:15:44.620
...without making any genuine attempt at our survival ?

00:15:44.620 --> 00:15:45.860
"Plans" ?

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:50.370
Is it such a great "plan" to listen to one soldier's hogwash and expose our ship to such danger ?

00:15:50.370 --> 00:15:54.140
Military rank and knowledge or talents are two different things.

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:57.500
Your vision is only as wide as the width of the military world.

00:15:58.150 --> 00:15:59.890
That's funny.

00:15:59.890 --> 00:16:03.270
An aristocrat kiddy is telling me I'm ignorant and inexperienced.

00:16:03.270 --> 00:16:07.400
Do you think commoners have always
withstood more adversity than aristocrats ?

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:10.700
You're just a spoiled brat who became a LTJG at age 16 due to preferential treatment...

00:16:10.700 --> 00:16:12.800
...because your sister
is the Emperor's favorite.

00:16:12.800 --> 00:16:15.100
Where have you earned the right to say stuff like that ?!

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.900
What do you know about my life ?

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:19.830
This isn't good !

00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:21.400
An enemy ship is approaching us !

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:26.070
If they keep their course, it's highly
possible that our ship will be detected.

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:28.930
About how long do we have
until we are are discovered ?

00:16:28.930 --> 00:16:30.370
Approximately 15 minutes.

00:16:30.370 --> 00:16:33.370
Seven minutes till the expected start time of the operation.

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:34.910
How are the engine repairs ?

00:16:34.910 --> 00:16:36.230
At 30%.

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:37.250
Continue with the task.

00:16:37.250 --> 00:16:38.500
That's insane !

00:16:38.500 --> 00:16:43.150
If we move now, we'll further
risk being discovered !

00:16:43.150 --> 00:16:45.800
Even if we don't move,
we'll be discovered.

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:47.270
Prepare to retract the anchors !

00:16:47.800 --> 00:16:48.770
Stop it !

00:16:48.770 --> 00:16:51.010
If you don't stop, I'll kill him !

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:54.600
Sir, please stop.

00:16:54.600 --> 00:16:58.250
You were the star of
hope for us commoners.

00:16:58.250 --> 00:17:00.950
And just who betrayed me ?

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:02.700
You're reaping
what you sowed.

00:17:02.700 --> 00:17:04.140
I didn't betray you.

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:07.340
We were just trying our best to think of a way to survive.

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:09.780
You're just a soldier.
Why do you have to "think" ?

00:17:09.780 --> 00:17:14.540
You soldiers are just hands and arms.
"Thinking" is a task of the elite officers.

00:17:14.540 --> 00:17:17.050
So that's your real opinion.

00:17:17.050 --> 00:17:17.850
It is.

00:17:18.350 --> 00:17:21.370
That's why I became an officer.

00:17:21.370 --> 00:17:25.820
I wanted nothing to do with being drafted and starting as a junior soldier just because I'm a commoner !

00:17:25.820 --> 00:17:29.810
For those who are content in such a
predicament, they have no need to think.

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:31.210
And no right to think.

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:34.370
They should just keep their mouths shut and follow my orders !

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:37.180
So you weren't a representative of the commoners after all ?

00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:39.250
Who said that ?

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:41.090
Me, the representative
of the commoners ?

00:17:41.090 --> 00:17:42.280
Don't kid yourself.

00:17:42.280 --> 00:17:44.810
I'm not a loser like all of you !

00:17:45.870 --> 00:17:47.200
Loser...?

00:17:47.750 --> 00:17:51.140
Listen, military ranks are
different from class ranks !

00:17:51.140 --> 00:17:54.640
If you get promoted in the military, you can order around aristocratic subordinates !

00:17:54.640 --> 00:17:56.400
That's what it means to "win" !

00:17:57.470 --> 00:18:00.700
So, Musel, I won't forgive you !

00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:01.950
You're a Lieutenant Junior Grade !

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:03.460
I'm a Lieutenant !

00:18:03.460 --> 00:18:06.580
All you need to do
is follow my orders !

00:18:06.580 --> 00:18:07.630
I refuse.

00:18:07.630 --> 00:18:09.250
What ?

00:18:09.250 --> 00:18:13.070
As an officer, I am entrusted with
the lives of the soldiers on this ship.

00:18:13.070 --> 00:18:16.550
I cannot let any of
them die for no reason.

00:18:16.550 --> 00:18:20.960
I believe it is best not to return command of this ship to you at the present time.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:25.280
If that's an act of mutiny, I will willingly suffer such dishonor !

00:18:32.910 --> 00:18:36.980
Brother, regardless of what happens to me, please just help the Chief Navigator !

00:18:36.980 --> 00:18:40.260
I support LTJG Musel,
even if I have to die !

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:42.850
Rolf, you...

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:44.800
I won't let Rolf die alone.

00:18:44.800 --> 00:18:47.960
If the First Officer interferes with LTJG Musel, I will, too{help Lt. Jg. Musel}.

00:18:47.960 --> 00:18:49.490
Me, too !

00:18:49.690 --> 00:18:50.400
I will, too !

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:51.230
I'll do the same !

00:18:51.230 --> 00:18:53.620
I'll support LTJG Musel.

00:18:54.860 --> 00:18:56.470
You were listening...?

00:18:56.470 --> 00:19:00.160
We told everyone the
situation up to this point, Sir.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:03.800
It seems you have no allies, at least among the soldiers.

00:19:05.030 --> 00:19:06.580
You bastards...

00:19:19.230 --> 00:19:20.160
You...

00:19:22.460 --> 00:19:24.040
If only you didn't exist...!

00:19:38.520 --> 00:19:39.050
Rolf...

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:42.360
Rolf !

00:19:45.380 --> 00:19:47.500
Brother, I'm sorry.

00:19:47.820 --> 00:19:48.700
Rolf...

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:49.810
Rolf !

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:52.740
Lieutenant Junior Grade....

00:19:55.800 --> 00:19:57.970
You make a good drawing subject.

00:19:57.970 --> 00:20:00.260
I wanted to ask you
to be a model...

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:03.420
Rolf...

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:04.340
Rolf...

00:20:04.940 --> 00:20:05.870
R...Rolf...

00:20:06.420 --> 00:20:07.440
R...Rolf...

00:20:10.710 --> 00:20:11.690
Rolf !

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:20.760
You...!

00:20:23.260 --> 00:20:25.000
For doing what you did...!

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:34.130
Hold it, both of you.

00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:35.540
Put down your guns.

00:20:40.650 --> 00:20:41.500
Captain !

00:20:45.900 --> 00:20:47.880
He's already passed away.

00:20:47.880 --> 00:20:48.940
I see.

00:20:48.940 --> 00:20:50.440
It's unfortunate.

00:20:50.440 --> 00:20:51.540
Take care of him.

00:20:55.630 --> 00:21:00.350
For starters, because I
faint-heartedly fell to injury...

00:21:00.350 --> 00:21:03.350
...I put both of you
through unnecessary trouble.

00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:05.050
I must apologize for this.

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:10.900
And it developed into such a serious conflict and ended up resulting in a casualty...

00:21:11.880 --> 00:21:14.690
I still can't return
to the rigors of duty...

00:21:14.690 --> 00:21:16.400
...therefore, Lieutenant Junior Grade Musel...

00:21:17.400 --> 00:21:21.040
...I officially appoint you as the
interim captain of this ship.

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:22.620
I want you to take
command from now on.

00:21:24.940 --> 00:21:27.400
Captain, you made your decision
because you both are aristocrats...?

00:21:30.170 --> 00:21:32.890
First Officer, that has
nothing to do with this.

00:21:32.890 --> 00:21:36.340
You're too hung
up on the class system.

00:21:36.340 --> 00:21:41.620
What I appreciate are his desire to rescue this ship and his poised judgment.

00:21:41.620 --> 00:21:45.090
First Officer, I ask you to
cooperate with the interim captain.

00:21:47.560 --> 00:21:49.660
I'm counting on you two...

00:21:52.480 --> 00:21:53.240
Captain !

00:21:54.030 --> 00:21:55.150
Take him to 
sick bay again !

00:21:56.350 --> 00:21:58.800
This is why I said he
needed complete rest.

00:22:00.300 --> 00:22:02.960
Try not to put any more
stress on the Captain !

00:22:02.960 --> 00:22:04.800
Anything more, and I won't
be held responsible !

00:22:09.400 --> 00:22:10.230
Lord Reinhard...

00:22:10.770 --> 00:22:11.600
I know.

00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:14.140
We may have underestimated the Captain.

00:22:17.940 --> 00:22:19.240
Just as you heard.

00:22:19.240 --> 00:22:22.750
I have officially been appointed by the
Captain to assume command of the ship.

00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:23.750
I presume there is no disagreement ?

00:22:26.640 --> 00:22:27.650
First Officer.

00:22:29.380 --> 00:22:30.270
I understand.

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:33.810
Then, we will continue our operation !

00:22:34.990 --> 00:22:36.500
15 seconds.

00:22:36.500 --> 00:22:37.600
Prepare for the operation quickly !

00:22:50.350 --> 00:22:53.980
Official command of the ship
finally fell into Reinhard's hands.

00:22:53.980 --> 00:22:56.830
But the true test was still to come.

00:22:57.660 --> 00:23:00.700
Retract the anchors and prepare for freefall !

00:23:00.350 --> 00:23:03.800
To be continued

